Verdict: PASS. The fix for #1169 does what the task asked. I wrote the verdict to session_plan/eval_task_2.md.

• The fix: run_git and run_git_in_dir now share one decoder, git_stdout, which trims only the end of git's output. The first line of git status --porcelain now keeps its leading space, so  M Cargo.toml stays an unstaged edit instead of turning into a staged M Cargo.toml. This is the narrow helper-level fix the task preferred.
• The tests: the new tests in src/git_porcelain_tests.rs run real git in a temporary repo and feed the helper's actual output to the parsers:
  • The banner counts give 0 staged and 2 modified.
  • /git stage gets the full paths Cargo.toml and src/lib.rs.
  • A one-character filename a on the first line survives.
  • A staged-only first line (M  x) still counts as staged.
  • The first lines of /git status --short and git diff --stat keep their alignment.
• Callers that might have relied on the old trim: I spot-checked the ones whose output can start with a space or a blank line. The --shortstat reader in commands_spawn.rs trims the text itself. The log --name-only --pretty=format: readers in commands_risk.rs and commands_map.rs skip blank lines. None of these needed the leading trim.
• Wiring: the new decoder and the test file are both hooked up. The size limit for git.rs in tests/module_size.rs went from 2032 to 2037 lines, with a comment explaining why. There's a CHANGELOG entry.

The harness had already run build and tests, so I didn't re-run them, and I didn't run the binary to reproduce the banner myself. The tests do push the real helper's output through the banner's own counting function.

One cleanup note: the commit message is missing the "probed N of M call sites" census line the task asked for.
